rectangle "MORE THAN ENOUGH\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>" <<Boundary-TU9SRSBUSEFOIEVOT1VHSA==>> {
  rectangle "Simulation Core\n<size:16>[Container: JavaScript modules (browser + Node)]</size>" <<Boundary-U2ltdWxhdGlvbiBDb3Jl>> {
    rectangle "==Living Crystal\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nExtends the existing endless world, inventory, clock and commands. New-world geography, local indexed heat/light, damage, tending, renewable wild colonies, protected material condition/storage/transfer, and the first dormant-machine repair. Original texture-pack buildings gain physical shutters/fans and condition marks in the existing row renderer. Legacy terrain/rules and saves are retained." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsQ29yZSBFbmdpbmU=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.SimulationCore.LivingCrystal
    rectangle "==Layered World\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nCoordinates and key packing (x, y, z), tile rules as data (TILE_INFO), and chunked terrain: the forest surface at z = 0 from noise octaves, solid geology below with one shaft per chunk. Chunks are generated lazily and LRU-cached; player edits (richness mods), per-layer fog and the holes between layers live outside the cache. Explored chunks and observed resource types have derived spatial indexes, including one/two-unit reserve masks that remove exhausted deposits from searches; Map-compatible prop mutation epochs invalidate charger candidates." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsQ29yZSBFbmdpbmU=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.SimulationCore.LayeredWorld
    rectangle "==State and Saves\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\ncreateState() builds the state; serialize/deserialize write and validate a JSON save (its format is WORLD_FORMAT in format.js, frozen so every world is kept; saves from format 10 on load, and the browser sets aside, never overwrites, one it can't read). state.events is transient and never saved." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsQ29yZSBFbmdpbmU=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.SimulationCore.StateandSaves
    rectangle "==Simulation Step\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nstep(s, dt): production, logistics, abundance income and battery; movement and fog reveal. Browser and AUTO hosts enable cumulative solo production after Logistics: grouped rates, cached counts/mastery, command/query settlements, and buffer snapshots at saves or rate changes. Visual events query nearby tile buckets. Cultivation runs local environment deadlines at 250ms in the same canonical step. Battery intervals support quiet-tick batching and reuse nearby charger candidates with exact range and daylight checks. Reveal compares exact circle row intervals and visits newly covered edges. Resource streams settle together with targeted manual balance updates. Variable-step/shared callers and extreme arithmetic retain the legacy economy." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsQ29yZSBFbmdpbmU=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.SimulationCore.SimulationStep
    rectangle "==Actions\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nHarvest (gather deposits on the surface, dig rock underground), Trail sweep targets, collect, and build; plus travel between layers through holes (dig down from the forest, climb up through the ceiling, drop through holes and shafts). All work on the player's own layer." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsQ29yZSBFbmdpbmU=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.SimulationCore.Actions
    rectangle "==AUTO Brain\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nnextIntent(s, mind): legal player actions from explored terrain, remembered observations, visible mine glints, own resources and public rules. Integer A* treats unseen underground rock as an assumption and replans after normal revelation, without inspecting hidden geology. Unseen chargers, ladders, shores and tunnel props cannot steer decisions. Prices building repayment against required upgrades; mining is a fallback only when surface acquisition is unavailable, includes passive income and return travel and targets useful observed finds. Waits at Embark, and never spends Insight in shared worlds. Selected known chargers alone authorize charging decisions. Manual holds share AUTO cadence. Pure: mind caches observations and routes." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsQ29yZSBFbmdpbmU=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.SimulationCore.AUTOBrain
    rectangle "==Stockpile\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nWhat you own as piles around home, on a logarithmic scale: one pile per unit of the two leading digits (at most 18 per resource), each power of ten its own kind; from 10^7 a pile covers a square of tiles one wider per power, as far as its slot allows. Home ground is a square laid out like a town: roads cross in the middle and each resource owns a block with fixed slots (the leading digit in the corner by the crossroads, the second along the outer edges), so nothing stands outside home ground or on another pile. Pure: only a picture of the inventory." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsQ29yZSBFbmdpbmU=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.SimulationCore.Stockpile
    rectangle "==Catalog\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nEverything that exists in the game, by the id a texture pack knows it by: tiles, resources, buildings, the wanderer, marks, buttons, upgrades, perks and colours, each with what it does and the slots a pack can fill. Built from the other content tables, so a new tile or upgrade can't go undocumented." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsQ29yZSBFbmdpbmU=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.SimulationCore.Catalog
    rectangle "==Economy and Upgrades\n<size:16>[Component: JavaScript]</size>\n\nContent tables, costs and multipliers, and one registry of every purchase (tools, refineries, the Abundance Engine, unlocks, perks) that buying, the progression map and the sheet all share; the ledger (income lines, spending at today's prices, payback in seconds of your own income). Stoneworks supplies a non-stacking same-owner quarry bonus within two tiles. A derived tile index caches service links per layout; both scalar and event economies use instance rates. Experimental solo depots use an eight-tile same-owner/layer collection index; overlapping depots never duplicate transfers. Also embark/prestige and the goal track." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQsQ29yZSBFbmdpbmU=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.SimulationCore.EconomyandUpgrades
  }

  rectangle "==Web Application\n<size:16>[Container: HTML/CSS/JavaScript modules]</size>\n\nThe presentation layer (index.html, style.css, src/game/). Owns the DOM, the canvas, input, audio, HUD and sheets, and localStorage. Reads state from the Simulation Core every frame and changes it only through the Core's exports." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication
}

